VVEERRSSIIOONNSS
       Unlike iinneett__aattoonn(3) and iinneett__aaddddrr(3), iinneett__ppttoonn() supports IPv6
       addresses.  On the other hand, iinneett__ppttoonn() accepts only IPv4 addresses
       in dotted‐decimal notation, whereas iinneett__aattoonn(3) and iinneett__aaddddrr(3) allow
       the more general numbers‐and‐dots notation (hexadecimal and octal
       number formats, and formats that don’t require all four bytes to be
       explicitly written).  For an interface that handles both IPv6
       addresses, and IPv4 addresses in numbers‐and‐dots notation, see
       ggeettaaddddrriinnffoo(3).

